.TH BOOTLOGGER 1.SH NAMEbootlogger \- record when the system started.SH SYNOPSIS\fBbootlogger\fR.SH DESCRIPTION\fBbootlogger\fRwrites the current date and time to\fB/dd/SYS/bootlog\fR,\fRand prints nothing.  Run from the startup file it keeps a record ofevery time the machine came up; run by hand it records the time you ranit.  Read the log to see what it did.  By F. R. Schmitt..SH FILES.TP 12\fB/dd/SYS/bootlog\fRthe log..SH NOTESNeeds Microware's\fBcio\fR.\fR